{"baseRefName":"main","body":"## Unresolved result\nKirby Problem 4.36 remains unsolved after two substantive approaches. This package preserves the exact full homotopy 2-type and actual 2-knot-complement realization requirements.\n\nIt records standard duality/group-cohomology deductions and a finite amalgam block computation. The remaining gaps are explicit: no required degree-one map of pairs is realized from the unmarked 2-type, and no pair of actual exteriors with identical full 2-types but different homotopy types is constructed.\n\n## Independent review\nSeparate adversarial review: PASS for the scoped partial deductions and unresolved disposition, with unchanged proof SHA-256 `69a3ffb7b6c2ba3bf1a4df8d7d83960d66095db9d175d78cfe49e2324aac1a71`.\n- 507 author assertions reproduced exactly\n- 29,933 independent exact controls pass\n- The complete review, snapshot and reproduction files are included\n\nThis is independent AI review, not formal verification or human peer review. No new theorem or historical priority is claimed.\n\n## Source safeguards\nThe latest different-k-invariant examples are not same-2-type counterexamples; boundary-surjectivity results do not cover noncyclic knot groups. The limited retrieval of the 1983 quasi-aspherical paper is disclosed. Mathematical and source-scope caveats are retained in full.\n","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-09-30T05:35:32Z","authors":[{"email":"me@aleckriebel.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","login":"AlecKriebel","name":"AlecKriebel"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-30T05:35:32Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Record exact 2-knot two-type question and prior-attempt gate","oid":"1207a508a3b66ef0ae1ef95cc2555fcf82ef3274"},{"authoredDate":"2026-09-30T05:50:47Z","authors":[{"email":"me@aleckriebel.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","login":"AlecKriebel","name":"AlecKriebel"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-30T05:50:47Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Document stalled Kirby 4.36 routes and exact obstruction checks","oid":"fe2fc529e6a8c539a7e110d1c80a43818bdc492d"},{"authoredDate":"2026-09-30T06:16:26Z","authors":[{"email":"me@aleckriebel.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","login":"AlecKriebel","name":"AlecKriebel"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-30T06:16:26Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Add independent review of stalled two-knot deductions","oid":"23069ca8679d489a405067d6fc479154761dcccc"},{"authoredDate":"2026-09-30T06:20:22Z","authors":[{"email":"me@aleckriebel.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","login":"AlecKriebel","name":"Alec Kriebel"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-30T06:20:22Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Update queue status for 2912 with reviewed PR outcome","oid":"c772dc5b851ec91da9d46d534577609e5d3ca389"}],"headRefName":"dot/math-2912","headRefOid":"c772dc5b851ec91da9d46d534577609e5d3ca389","isDraft":true,"number":44,"state":"OPEN","title":"2912: reviewed two-knot obstruction audit; full problem unresolved","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/44"}
